cla_mmrs, dst_sink_mmrs: state that every trDstRamData read advances the pointer and that an EAP set beats its w2c clear

trDstRamRPLow and trDstRamData said the read pointer moves only on a read
that returns unread data, but the sink advances it on every read; an empty
read returns 0 and still moves it. CDbgEapStatus did not say that a status
bit whose relation still holds on the current node is set again in the
cycle of a w2c write, so the write leaves it at 1.

Recorded as a patch so the hand-mirrored upstream/ tree stays
reproducible from the vendored spec plus patches/ applied in order.
diff --git a/rtl/mmr/spec/cla_mmrs.yml b/rtl/mmr/spec/cla_mmrs.yml
diff --git a/rtl/mmr/spec/cla_mmrs.yml b/rtl/mmr/spec/cla_mmrs.yml
index c2ed4de29..9bec20b08 100644
--- a/rtl/mmr/spec/cla_mmrs.yml
+++ b/rtl/mmr/spec/cla_mmrs.yml
@@ -3214,7 +3214,11 @@ c_dbg_eap_status:
       action was taken (ex: NMI ISR needs to know which of the EAP triggered the NMI).
       A w2c write does not release a debug interrupt while EnableEap is set: the EAP
       holds the interrupt and the write clears only the status bit. To release it, clear
-      EnableEap, then write the w2c bit.'
+      EnableEap, then write the w2c bit. A status bit sets in every cycle in which its
+      EAP relation holds while its node is current and EnableEap is set, and that set
+      takes priority over a w2c write in the same cycle, which then leaves the bit at
+      1. Write the w2c bit once the relation is false, the node is no longer current
+      or EnableEap is clear.'
     RESET_PORT: reset_n_warm_ovrride
     HW_READ: CLA
     HW_WRITE: CLA
diff --git a/rtl/mmr/spec/dst_sink_mmrs.yml b/rtl/mmr/spec/dst_sink_mmrs.yml
index e6ab2de16..5b52f4ef2 100644
--- a/rtl/mmr/spec/dst_sink_mmrs.yml
+++ b/rtl/mmr/spec/dst_sink_mmrs.yml
@@ -284,8 +284,9 @@ trDstRamRPLow:
     RESET_VALUE: '0'
     LEGAL_VALUE: ''
     DESCRIPTION: Read pointer, in 32-bit words; bits [31:2] of the byte address of
-      the word the next trDstRamData read returns. Each trDstRamData read that returns
-      unread data advances it by one word, and from trDstRamLimitLow it wraps to trDstRamStartLow.
+      the word the next trDstRamData read returns. Every trDstRamData read advances it
+      by one word, including a read while the RAM holds no unread data, and from
+      trDstRamLimitLow it wraps to trDstRamStartLow.
     HW_WRITE: DST_SINK
     SW_WRITE: W
     SW_READ: R
@@ -336,9 +337,11 @@ trDstRamData:
     FIELDS_RANGE: '31:0'
     RESET_VALUE: '0'
     LEGAL_VALUE: ''
-    DESCRIPTION: Reading launches a trace-RAM read at trDstRamRPLow. When the RAM
-      holds unread data, the read returns that 32-bit word and advances trDstRamRPLow;
-      otherwise the pointer does not move.
+    DESCRIPTION: Reading returns the 32-bit word at trDstRamRPLow and advances
+      trDstRamRPLow by one word. A read while the RAM holds no unread data returns 0
+      and still advances the pointer, so software that polls this register while the
+      sink is empty skips words it has not yet received. Read only while trDstRamWPLow
+      differs from trDstRamRPLow or trDstRamWrap is set.
     SW_READ: R
     SW_TYPE: ''
 scratch_lo:
